{
 "chapter": "gceal-further-maths-calculus-ext",
 "lessons": [
  {
   "id": "gceal-further-maths-differential-equations-2",
   "title": "Second-order linear differential equations",
   "minutes": 25,
   "programRef": "Cameroon GCE Board — Advanced Level Further Mathematics syllabus (Upper Sixth part; scope to be checked against the official text)",
   "status": "draft",
   "author": "CastBridge (AI draft)",
   "source": "Original writing following the Cameroonian curriculum; to be reviewed by a teacher",
   "objectives": [
    "Solve $ay''+by'+cy=0$ using the auxiliary equation",
    "Find particular integrals for simple right-hand sides",
    "Apply initial conditions"
   ],
   "prerequisites": [],
   "exercises": [
    "gceal-further-maths-calculus-ext-e01",
    "gceal-further-maths-calculus-ext-e02",
    "gceal-further-maths-calculus-ext-e03",
    "gceal-further-maths-calculus-ext-e04",
    "gceal-further-maths-calculus-ext-e05",
    "gceal-further-maths-calculus-ext-e06"
   ],
   "selfCheck": [
    "gceal-further-maths-differential-equations-2-q1",
    "gceal-further-maths-differential-equations-2-q2",
    "gceal-further-maths-differential-equations-2-q3",
    "gceal-further-maths-differential-equations-2-q4",
    "gceal-further-maths-differential-equations-2-q5"
   ],
   "reviewNotes": [
    "Whether this topic is on the Cameroon GCE Board Further Mathematics syllabus is to be confirmed: it is standard A-Level Further Maths content.",
    "Resonance cases and systems of equations not included.",
    "Syllabus references, scope and level of difficulty are to be checked against the official text; all facts, formulas and worked examples to be verified by a teacher before release."
   ],
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "formule",
     "title": "Homogeneous equation",
     "md": "$ay''+by'+cy=0$ has auxiliary equation $am^2+bm+c=0$. Distinct real roots $m_1,m_2$: $y=Ae^{m_1x}+Be^{m_2x}$. Repeated root $m$: $y=(A+Bx)e^{mx}$. Complex roots $p\\pm qi$: $y=e^{px}(A\\cos qx+B\\sin qx)$. $A$ and $B$ are arbitrary constants."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "methode",
     "title": "Non-homogeneous equation",
     "md": "$ay''+by'+cy=f(x)$: general solution = complementary function (the solution of the homogeneous equation) + particular integral (PI). Try a PI of the same form as $f(x)$: constant for a constant, $px+q$ for a linear $f$, $pe^{kx}$ for $e^{kx}$, $p\\cos kx+q\\sin kx$ for trig. If the trial is already in the complementary function multiply by $x$."
    },
    {
     "type": "illustration",
     "figure": {
      "kind": "plot",
      "xmin": 0,
      "xmax": 1.5,
      "ymin": -5,
      "ymax": 95,
      "grid": 1,
      "w": 400,
      "h": 260,
      "curves": [
       {
        "expr": "exp(3x)-exp(x)",
        "color": "blue"
       }
      ],
      "points": [
       {
        "x": 1,
        "y": 17.367255094728623,
        "label": "(1, 17.4)",
        "color": "red"
       }
      ],
      "segments": [],
      "xlabel": "x"
     },
     "caption": "The solution $y=e^{3x}-e^x$ of $y''-4y'+3y=0$ with $y(0)=0$, $y'(0)=2$ grows rapidly.",
     "alt": "Curve starting at the origin with gradient 2 and rising steeply to about 17.4 at x=1."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "methode",
     "title": "Initial conditions",
     "md": "Two conditions (for example $y(0)$ and $y'(0)$) fix $A$ and $B$. Differentiate the general solution, substitute $x=0$ into both $y$ and $y'$, and solve the two equations."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "pieges",
     "title": "Common mistakes",
     "md": "Applying the conditions to the complementary function before adding the PI. Forgetting the factor $x$ for repeated roots. Solving $y'=\\ldots$ conditions with the wrong derivative of $e^{mx}$ (it is $me^{mx}$)."
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Example 1",
     "statement": "Solve $y''-5y'+6y=0$ with $y(0)=1$, $y'(0)=0$.",
     "steps": [
      "Auxiliary: $m^2-5m+6=0$, $m=2,3$: $y=Ae^{2x}+Be^{3x}$.",
      "$y(0)=A+B=1$; $y'(0)=2A+3B=0$. So $B=-2$, $A=3$."
     ],
     "answer": "$y=3e^{2x}-2e^{3x}$"
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Example 2",
     "statement": "Solve $y''+4y=0$ and $y''-3y'+2y=4$.",
     "steps": [
      "$m^2+4=0$, $m=\\pm2i$: $y=A\\cos2x+B\\sin2x$.",
      "For the second: $m=1,2$, complementary function $Ae^x+Be^{2x}$. Try the PI $y=c$: $2c=4$, $c=2$. General solution $y=Ae^x+Be^{2x}+2$."
     ],
     "answer": "$y=A\\cos2x+B\\sin2x$; $y=Ae^x+Be^{2x}+2$"
    }
   ],
