  {
   "id": "gceal-further-maths-series-further",
   "title": "Further series and limits",
   "minutes": 25,
   "programRef": "Cameroon GCE Board — Advanced Level Further Mathematics syllabus (Upper Sixth part; scope to be checked against the official text)",
   "status": "draft",
   "author": "CastBridge (AI draft)",
   "source": "Original writing following the Cameroonian curriculum; to be reviewed by a teacher",
   "objectives": [
    "Expand $(1+x)^n$ for rational $n$",
    "Find series of products and quotients such as $\\tan x$",
    "Evaluate limits using series"
   ],
   "prerequisites": [],
   "exercises": [
    "gceal-further-maths-calculus-ext-e13",
    "gceal-further-maths-calculus-ext-e14",
    "gceal-further-maths-calculus-ext-e15",
    "gceal-further-maths-calculus-ext-e16",
    "gceal-further-maths-calculus-ext-e17",
    "gceal-further-maths-calculus-ext-e18"
   ],
   "selfCheck": [
    "gceal-further-maths-series-further-q1",
    "gceal-further-maths-series-further-q2",
    "gceal-further-maths-series-further-q3",
    "gceal-further-maths-series-further-q4",
    "gceal-further-maths-series-further-q5"
   ],
   "reviewNotes": [
    "Whether this topic is on the Cameroon GCE Board Further Mathematics syllabus is to be confirmed: it is standard A-Level Further Maths content.",
    "Syllabus references, scope and level of difficulty are to be checked against the official text; all facts, formulas and worked examples to be verified by a teacher before release."
   ],
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "formule",
     "title": "Binomial series",
     "md": "For any rational $n$ and $|x|<1$: $(1+x)^n=1+nx+\\frac{n(n-1)}{2!}x^2+\\frac{n(n-1)(n-2)}{3!}x^3+\\cdots$. Example: $\\sqrt{1+x}=1+\\frac x2-\\frac{x^2}{8}+\\frac{x^3}{16}-\\cdots$ and $\\frac{1}{1+x}=1-x+x^2-\\cdots$. For $(a+bx)^n$ factor out $a^n$ first."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "methode",
     "title": "Products, quotients, composites",
     "md": "Multiply or divide the standard series ($e^x$, $\\sin x$, $\\cos x$, $\\ln(1+x)$) and keep terms up to the required power. For $\\tan x=\\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}$: $\\left(x-\\frac{x^3}{6}\\right)\\left(1+\\frac{x^2}{2}+\\cdots\\right)=x+\\frac{x^3}{3}+\\cdots$"
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "methode",
     "title": "Limits",
     "md": "To find $\\lim_{x\\to0}\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)}$ when both $\\to0$, expand numerator and denominator in series and divide by the lowest power of $x$. Example: $\\frac{e^x-1-x}{x^2}=\\frac{\\frac{x^2}{2}+\\frac{x^3}{6}+\\cdots}{x^2}\\to\\frac{1}{2}$."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "pieges",
     "title": "Common mistakes",
     "md": "Using the binomial series outside $|x|<1$ (for example for $(1+x)^{1/2}$ at $x=3$). Dropping a term of the lower order that does not cancel. Mixing degrees and radians: the series for $\\sin x$ need radians."
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Example 1",
     "statement": "Expand $\\sqrt{1+x}$ to $x^3$ and estimate $\\sqrt{1.02}$.",
     "steps": [
      "$n=\\frac{1}{2}$: $1+\\frac x2+\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}{2}x^2+\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\left(-\\frac{3}{2}\\right)}{6}x^3=1+\\frac x2-\\frac{x^2}{8}+\\frac{x^3}{16}$.",
      "With $x=0.02$: $1+0.01-0.00005=1.00995$ (true value 1.009950)."
     ],
     "answer": "$1+\\frac x2-\\frac{x^2}{8}+\\frac{x^3}{16}$; $\\sqrt{1.02}\\approx1.00995$"
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Example 2",
     "statement": "Find $\\lim_{x\\to0}\\frac{\\sin x-x}{x^3}$.",
     "steps": [
      "$\\sin x-x=-\\frac{x^3}{6}+\\frac{x^5}{120}-\\cdots$",
      "Divide by $x^3$: $-\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{x^2}{120}-\\cdots\\to-\\frac{1}{6}$."
     ],
     "answer": "$-\\frac{1}{6}$",
     "figure": {
      "kind": "plot",
      "xmin": -1.2,
      "xmax": 1.2,
      "ymin": -3,
      "ymax": 3,
      "grid": 1,
      "w": 400,
      "h": 260,
      "curves": [
       {
        "expr": "sin(x)/cos(x)",
        "color": "blue",
        "label": "tan x"
       },
       {
